Dear all,

I came across a minor issue using the morpho.disparity function in the latest version of geomorph.

So taking the example from help file, if one run the following code that include covariates (a complex model), then a list is returned with extractable objects.

data(plethodon)
Y.gpa<-gpagen(plethodon$land, print.progress = FALSE)    #GPA-alignment
gdf <- geomorph.data.frame(Y.gpa, species = plethodon$species, site = plethodon$site)

MD <- morphol.disparity(coords ~ Csize + species*site, groups= ~ species,
                        data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)

MD$Procrustes.var

But, if we now make the model a bit simpler and exclude covariates, then even though the disparity calculation is performed, the MD object will return as NULL.
MD <- morphol.disparity(coords ~ 1, data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)
MD

It is an easy fix though and simply require that an extra function (i.e. 'return') to be added to the script.
...
if (is.null(groups)) {
    pv.obs <- pv
    return(pv.obs)
