For non-GM data I would not call them Procrustes variances, but they are fully equivalent. Essentially this comes from using the term "Procrustes distance" as an equivalent to the Euclidean distance of each observation from the group´s centroid calculated over superimposed coordinates projected to tangent space. See chapter 12, Disparity and Variation, in Zelditch et al. 2012 Geometric Morphometrics for Biologists for the formulae and correspondence between variance metrics.

